WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.541
hurried through the Metro City subway station.

2
00:00:14.561 --> 00:00:16.962
"Out of my way!"

3
00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:18.122
a man said.

4
00:00:18.142 --> 00:00:22.844
"I'm late for work!"

5
00:00:22.864 --> 00:00:24.465
A young woman walked into the station.

6
00:00:26.006 --> 00:00:27.386
She had a violin and a hat.

7
00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.508
She placed the hat on the floor.

8
00:00:33.052 --> 00:00:35.453
Then she ran her bow across the violin's strings.

9
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:38.794
Strange music filled the air.

10
00:00:39.794 --> 00:00:40.874
Everyone stopped walking.

11
00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:43.595
They all turned to stare at the young woman.

12
00:00:46.676 --> 00:00:49.516
Suddenly they pulled out their wallets and tossed them into the hat!

13
00:00:52.537 --> 00:00:55.598
"I can't wait for the concert to start," Mara said.

14
00:00:55.618 --> 00:00:59.119
"It'll be so cool to hear a real orchestra!"

15
00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:02.640
Roxy and her friends were at Metro City Park.

16
00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.838
The Metro City Symphony Orchestra was going to perform a concert.

17
00:01:08.219 --> 00:01:09.840
People sat on blankets on the grass.

18
00:01:10.941 --> 00:01:13.262
The musicians were onstage, tuning their instruments.

19
00:01:13.282 --> 00:01:18.406
"It's really warm today," Mara said.

20
00:01:18.426 --> 00:01:21.588
"Temperature affects musical instruments.

21
00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.929
That's why the musicians are checking them now."

22
00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:27.612
"I love live music," Terrell said.

23
00:01:27.632 --> 00:01:31.094
"I might join the school jazz band next year.

24
00:01:31.935 --> 00:01:33.536
I've been taking clarinet lessons."

25
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:35.521
Jack shrugged.

26
00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:37.742
"I guess the concert will be okay.

27
00:01:38.682 --> 00:01:40.643
I don't really like classical music though.

28
00:01:41.944 --> 00:01:43.145
I like rock and roll!"

29
00:01:44.345 --> 00:01:45.446
Jack jumped to his feet.

30
00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:49.268
He held up his hands as if he was holding a guitar.

31
00:01:50.148 --> 00:01:55.451
Everyone laughed as Jack danced around, pretending to be a rock star.

32
00:01:55.691 --> 00:02:00.274
"Well, I like classical music," Mara said.

33
00:02:00.294 --> 00:02:04.296
"The orchestra is going to play my favorite song today.

34
00:02:04.832 --> 00:02:07.634
I'm trying to learn it on the cello, but it's really hard."

35
00:02:08.655 --> 00:02:10.796
"Just keep practicing," Roxy said.

36
00:02:10.816 --> 00:02:12.718
"You'll get better and better.

37
00:02:13.798 --> 00:02:15.539
Maybe one day you'll perform here!"

38
00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:17.621
Mara laughed.

39
00:02:17.641 --> 00:02:19.422
"I doubt that!"

40
00:02:19.442 --> 00:02:24.506
"I know someone who's probably really good at music," Terrell said.

41
00:02:25.346 --> 00:02:26.427
Roxy rolled her eyes.

42
00:02:26.447 --> 00:02:28.208
"Ugh, Terrell.

43
00:02:28.608 --> 00:02:31.030
I doubt Rocket Girl even plays an instrument."

44
00:02:32.331 --> 00:02:33.512
Terrell looked surprised.

45
00:02:34.164 --> 00:02:36.626
"How did you know I was talking about Rocket Girl?"

46
00:02:37.587 --> 00:02:38.307
Roxy laughed.

47
00:02:39.448 --> 00:02:42.390
"Terrell, you always talk about Rocket Girl!"

48
00:02:44.872 --> 00:02:46.653
Just then Roxy's watch beeped.

49
00:02:48.314 --> 00:02:49.975
She looked around and then back at her friends.

50
00:02:49.995 --> 00:02:52.077
"I'll be right back.

51
00:02:52.997 --> 00:02:55.619
I, um, think I saw my neighbor.

52
00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.160
I want to go say hi."

53
00:02:59.162 --> 00:03:01.824
Roxy ducked behind a statue and pressed a button on her watch.

54
00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:04.773
Mayor Bloom's face appeared on the screen.

55
00:03:05.553 --> 00:03:06.474
"What's wrong, Mayor?"

56
00:03:06.894 --> 00:03:07.554
Roxy asked.

57
00:03:07.574 --> 00:03:11.496
"We need your help, Rocket Girl," Mayor Bloom said.

58
00:03:11.516 --> 00:03:14.498
"Mrs. Bun was having a fancy garden party.

59
00:03:15.378 --> 00:03:16.999
All of her guests were robbed!"

60
00:03:17.019 --> 00:03:20.361
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roxy said.

61
00:03:20.381 --> 00:03:22.422
"I'm on my way!"
